# ------------------------------------------------------------------ 8 listening 9-11
_L9 = [("Segment 1: preparedness", "Isa ang pribadong sektor sa mga aktibong nagsasagawa sa mga hakbang kaugnay sa paghahanda sa kalamidad. Partikular sa mga tinukoy ang epektibong ugnayan ng pamahalaan at ng pribadong sektor upang matulungan ang mga mamamayang naapektuhan ng kalamidad. Nakapaloob dito ang pagtaya sa pinsala at panganib na maaaring idulot ng pagtama ng mga ito at ang plano ukol sa paglilikas sa mga residente kung saan tuturuan ang mga pamilya na maghanda sa oras ng pangangailangan. Kailangan ding sumailalim sa training ang mga empleyado nang sila ay magamit ng kani-kanilang kumpanya upang makatulong sa disaster relief and response.", "The private sector is one of those actively carrying out steps related to preparing for calamities. Particularly mentioned is effective coordination between the government and the private sector to help the people affected by calamities. This includes estimating the damage and danger that these may cause when they strike, and the plan for evacuating residents, where families will be taught to prepare for the hour of need. Employees also need to undergo training so that they can be used by their respective companies to help in disaster relief and response."), ("Segment 2: response and rehabilitation", "Mahalaga ring tutukan ang mga programang tutugon sa pangmatagalang pangangailangan ng mga mamamayan at ang patuluyang pagmo-monitor sa mga ito. Kabilang sa mga ito ang konseptong Build Back Better na nagsasaad ng pagtatayo ng mga disaster resilient communities. Higit sa mga relief goods dapat din mapabilis ang mekanismo ng paghahatid ng tulong pinansyal sa pamamagitan ng electronic cash transfer upang agad na mapondohan ang mga programang pan-rehabitasyon sa mga komunidad na nasalanta. Dapat ring matugunan ang pagkukunan ng kabuhayan sa mga komunidad na napinsala at ang pamumuhunan sa mga apektadong lugar kung saan maaaring dumaloy ang malayang kalakalan na makatutulong para sa kanilang muling pagbangon matapos ng anumang hagupit ng kalikasan.", "It is also important to focus on programs that will respond to the long-term needs of the people and their continued monitoring. Among these is the concept of Build Back Better, which speaks of building disaster resilient communities. Beyond relief goods, the mechanism for delivering financial aid through electronic cash transfer should also be sped up, so that rehabilitation programs in the stricken communities can be funded right away. The source of livelihood in damaged communities must also be addressed, as well as investment in the affected places where free trade may flow, which will help their recovery after any lashing of nature.")]
_K9 = [["Preparedness", "Effective coordination between the government and the private sector; estimate the risk and damages that natural hazards can bring when they hit the area; plan the evacuation of residents, where families will be instructed to prepare for the hour of need; employees of the private sector will undergo training so that their companies can use them to help in disaster relief and response."], ["Response and rehabilitation", "Apply the concept of Build Back Better, which denotes building disaster resilient communities; expedite the mechanism of bringing financial aid through electronic cash transfer to fund rehabilitation programs in communities affected by calamities; provide sources of livelihood and investment requirements for communities affected by calamities."]]
_L10 = [("Segment 1", "Taos-pusong nagpapasalamat ang ating pamahalaan sa pandaigdigang komunidad sa patuloy na pagdaloy ng mga donasyon at suporta ng mga pamahalaan at pribadong organisasyon. Tuluy-tuloy at walang-humpay ang pagkilos ng lahat ng puwersa at ahensiya ng pamahalaan sa lahat ng larangan upang tumugon sa pangangailangan ng ating mga kababayan.", "Our government sincerely thanks the world community for the continuing flow of donations and support from governments and private organizations. All the forces and agencies of the government continue and do not stop acting in every field to respond to the needs of our countrymen."), ("Segment 2", "Ang mga prayoridad ng ating pamahalaan ay ang mga sumusunod. Una, ang agarang paghatid ng pagkain, tubig, gamot at tulong-medikal. Pangalawa, pagbibigay nang pansamantalang panuluyan para sa mga nawalan ng tahanan. Pangatlo, pagbabalik ng kuryente at linya ng komunikasyon. Pang-apat, panunumbalik ng transportasyong panlupa, pandagat at panghimpapawid. At panglima, pagbabalik ng mga pangunahing serbisyo-publiko na pinagtutulungan ng pambansa at lokal na pamahalaan doon sa mga lugar ng kalamidad na kung saan ang mga empleyado ng gobyerno ay biktima rin ng kalamidad.", "The priorities of our government are the following. First, the immediate delivery of food, water, medicine and medical aid. Second, giving temporary lodging for those who lost their homes. Third, the restoration of electricity and communication lines. Fourth, the restoration of land, sea and air transportation. And fifth, the restoration of basic public services, supported by the national and local governments in the calamity areas where government employees are also victims of the calamity."), ("Segment 3", "Nauunawaan natin ang pag-aalala sa kalagayan ng mga nasalanta ng kalamidad na hanggang ngayon ay hindi pa natutunton ang kanilang mga kamag-anak. Bente kwatro oras po ang operasyon ng pambansang network, ng PTV apat, Telebisyon ng Bayan at Radyo ng Bayan pitong daan at tatlumpu’t walong kilohertz para tanggapin ang mga panawagan ng mga mamamayan sa hindi pa makontak na mga kamag-anak, at upang tumugon sa mga mahahalagang pangangailangan. Maaari rin pong gamitin ang mga Facebook, Twitter at iba pang social media accounts ng PTV apat, Gov at work, at Philippine Information Agency o PIA.", "We understand the worry about the condition of those hit by the calamity whose relatives have still not been found. The national network, PTV 4, Telebisyon ng Bayan, and Radyo ng Bayan 738 kHz operate twenty-four hours to receive the pleas of citizens about relatives who cannot yet be contacted, and to respond to important needs. The Facebook, Twitter and other social media accounts of PTV 4, Gov at Work and the Philippine Information Agency, or PIA, may also be used.")]
_K10 = [["1. Who the Secretary thanked and why", "The Secretary expressed gratitude to the world community for the continuing flow of donations and support from different governments and private organizations."], ["2. What the government agencies are doing", "The government agencies in all fields act unceasingly with all their resources in order to respond to the needs of the people (their fellowmen)."], ["3. The five priorities", "(1) Immediate delivery of food, water, medicine and medical services; (2) provision of temporary lodging or shelter for those who lost their homes; (3) restoration of electric power and means of communication; (4) restoration of all means of transportation, land, air and sea; (5) restoration of primary public services under the cooperation of national and local governments in calamity areas where government employees are also victims."], ["4. The role of government television, radio and social media", "The government recognizes that many people worry about the situation and whereabouts of their relatives who are victims of the calamity. The Secretary informed the public that government television and radio stations operate 24 hours to receive citizen pleas or relay messages for relatives they want to contact and to respond to their important needs."]]
_L11 = [("Samantala, naka-alerto na rin ang Philippine Coastguard dahil sa inaasahang epekto ng Bagyong Isang.", "Meanwhile, the Philippine Coast Guard is also on alert because of the expected effect of Typhoon Isang."), ("Ayon kay Coastguard spokesman Arman Balillo, sinuspinde na ang paglalayag ng anumang uri ng sasakyang pandagat sa mga lugar na isinailalim sa storm signals.", "According to Coast Guard spokesman Arman Balillo, the sailing of any kind of vessel has been suspended in areas placed under storm signals."), ("Samantala, pinaalalahanan ng Coastguard ang mga residenteng nakatira malapit sa baybayin na maging alerto mula sa posibleng storm surge at biglaang pagtaas ng tubig.", "Meanwhile, the Coast Guard reminded residents living near the coast to be alert for a possible storm surge and sudden rise of water.")]
